00:00:33.938 --> 00:00:35.796
- [Voiceover] Kartik asks,
"What do you look for

00:00:35.796 --> 00:00:38.837
"when hiring creatives?"

00:00:38.837 --> 00:00:41.670
- Kartik, great question.

00:00:41.670 --> 00:00:44.073
Creatives are really interesting
hire here at VaynerMedia

00:00:44.073 --> 00:00:48.275
because in the agency
world, the creative process

00:00:48.275 --> 00:00:50.934
is very romantic, by my point of view.

00:00:50.934 --> 00:00:53.697
Meaning that, a lot of people
care about winning awards,

00:00:53.697 --> 00:00:56.773
a lot of people want to
make movies and TV shows,

00:00:56.773 --> 00:00:59.872
and for whatever reason they are

00:00:59.872 --> 00:01:01.568
now in the advertising
industry, and they're

00:01:01.568 --> 00:01:04.226
caring more about the craft than they are

00:01:04.226 --> 00:01:06.885
about the agenda, which is to sell coffee,

00:01:06.885 --> 00:01:08.428
to sell whatever this thing is.

00:01:08.428 --> 00:01:09.751
To sell phones.

00:01:09.751 --> 00:01:12.841
And so to me, what I'm
looking for in creatives

00:01:12.841 --> 00:01:15.643
are people that are very
creative, and still want to

00:01:15.643 --> 00:01:19.148
make the greatest creative
that they're capable of

00:01:19.148 --> 00:01:21.389
but also something that's
grounded in the fact

00:01:21.389 --> 00:01:23.142
that we're here to sell stuff.

00:01:23.142 --> 00:01:25.568
And if we don't ultimately move product

00:01:25.568 --> 00:01:28.784
or inspire people to donate, or make them

00:01:28.784 --> 00:01:32.568
aware about a cause,
we are not going to be

00:01:32.568 --> 00:01:34.286
fulfilling the duty at hand.

00:01:34.286 --> 00:01:36.968
And so I'm looking for
a level of practicality

00:01:36.968 --> 00:01:40.498
and a little hint of
2015 data understanding

00:01:40.498 --> 00:01:42.204
from my creatives, which
I think is a little bit

00:01:42.204 --> 00:01:44.274
of a different spin.

00:01:44.274 --> 00:01:45.854
