00:04:20.440 --> 00:04:22.077
Recognizing it's not for my 40 year old

00:04:22.077 --> 00:04:23.864
season ticket holder.

00:04:23.864 --> 00:04:26.500
So I would play to that psychology.

00:04:26.500 --> 00:04:28.322
- [Voiceover] Muscle Company asks,

00:04:28.322 --> 00:04:30.284
"How do you generate novel ideas in an

00:04:30.284 --> 00:04:32.942
"overpopulated, seemingly stale industry?

00:04:32.942 --> 00:04:36.402
"The fitness industry, for example."

00:04:36.402 --> 00:04:39.897
- The Muscle Company, I
kinda like saying that.

00:04:39.897 --> 00:04:43.820
The Muscle Company, I
always find the best way

00:04:43.820 --> 00:04:46.653
to attack an industry that you're in

00:04:46.653 --> 00:04:49.799
and is stale, and you want to innovate,

00:04:49.799 --> 00:04:52.434
by spending zero time in it.

00:04:52.434 --> 00:04:54.176
One little fun fact that
most people don't know

00:04:54.176 --> 00:04:57.658
is I spent an awful, excuse me,

00:04:57.658 --> 00:05:01.292
an extreme lack of time
within the wine industry

00:05:01.292 --> 00:05:02.998
and within the agency industry.

00:05:02.998 --> 00:05:04.240
I don't think I've ever been, I've been to

00:05:04.240 --> 00:05:06.539
six other agencies in
my life cuz they were

00:05:06.539 --> 00:05:07.398
meetings there.

00:05:07.398 --> 00:05:09.418
I know nothing about it. I read nothing

00:05:09.418 --> 00:05:11.995
about other agencies at Ad Age,

00:05:11.995 --> 00:05:13.899
spend no time asking
my senior people about

00:05:13.899 --> 00:05:15.931
what they did at other agencies.

00:05:15.931 --> 00:05:17.196
When I was in the wine
business, everyone was

00:05:17.196 --> 00:05:18.972
like, "You should go check
out this store in Dallas,

00:05:18.972 --> 00:05:21.096
"they're doing X," I'm
like, "I don't give a crap."

00:05:21.096 --> 00:05:24.138
For me, the way I've
always been innovative

00:05:24.138 --> 00:05:27.250
is lack of education, and I'm not joking.

00:05:27.250 --> 00:05:29.490
I tend to stay within myself
and what comes natural

00:05:29.490 --> 00:05:31.997
and two, I look to other industries.

00:05:31.997 --> 00:05:34.250
So if I were you, I
would be paying attention

00:05:34.250 --> 00:05:36.270
to what's happening in the food industry

00:05:36.270 --> 00:05:40.167
or in the rock-climbing industry or things

00:05:40.167 --> 00:05:43.348
completely left field
like hip-hop or sports

00:05:43.348 --> 00:05:45.867
or just stuff that has nothing to do with

00:05:45.867 --> 00:05:48.007
your industry, because the best way to

00:05:48.007 --> 00:05:49.713
stay within the zone and not innovate

00:05:49.713 --> 00:05:51.234
is pay attention to everybody else,

00:05:51.234 --> 00:05:54.090
because they're doing the same crap too.

